xactly; then verify separate serial units against fresh original execution.","tolerance":"0 differing scientific bytes, 0 missing or extra scientific files, identical stable relative paths. Exclude only predeclared volatile logs and timestamps.","independent_code":"New manifest and byte-comparison verifier; no independent docking implementation claimed."},"checks":["Before allocation, require frozen input/reference/output manifests and explicit permission-free access to supplied historical artifacts. Missing artifacts block execution.","Build four CPU unit manifests plus controller, exact-output verifier, process-tree resource recorder, allocation watchdog and compact exporter. CPU build target documented at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akiyamalab/MEGADOCK/9575280c875732553266e26adc607dd892b02616/doc/BUILD.md.","Initial original serial block must match frozen historical CPU artifacts; separate serial units must then match original serial block before concurrent arms begin.","Compare prepared PDB hashes, docking scientific records, complete final PDB files and scientific file inventories. Preserve original path obligations through isolated execution roots.","Generate and retain all 50 poses per case per block. Never compare only rank one or selected successful cases.","Hash shared inputs before and after every block; record unauthorized shared writes. Never normalize newly discovered differences after seeing results.","Measure complete block wall time through final pose creation; report docking-only time separately. Record CPU seconds, effective cores, CPU busy fraction, context switches, memory/thread peaks, shared-change counts and GPU activity.","Stop later probe arms immediately on baseline mismatch. Finish with original serial repeat as drift and repeatability control.","Interpret high busy without gain as evidence against unchanged-thread concurrency; low busy without gain motivates launch/I/O analysis. Thread reduction requires separate sealed follow-up."